REVE's mean and attention poolings come from one forward pass: `FoundationEmbeddingExtractor(extra_poolings=("attention",))` pools the same tokens again through the backend's new `pool_tokens`, into `extra_window_embeddings`, normalised like window vectors, and `write_recording_embeddings` writes each in a window file of its own label (`baseAttention`) whose `WindowPooling` names it. `write_recording_embeddings` now returns its paths keyed by `(label, view)`.
